WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.920
Speaker 1: Our friend Michael Cohen, Donald
Trump's former personal attorney, he seems

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:10.309
to be putting his foot down and saying, hey,
guys, either indict Trump or I'm out and I'm

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:11.780
going to stop cooperating.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.250
And I have to tell you, I sympathize with
Michael Cohen 100%.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.860
So let's go through what's going on.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:23.199
There's a good Daily Beast piece called The
Manhattan DA's Star Witness Indict Trump Now

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:27.199
or I'm Out the Pieces by Jose Pagliaro.

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:32.270
And it reads, If Manhattan prosecutors don't
indict former President Donald Trump with

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:37.370
the grand jury they've got in the next nine
days, the key witness investigators used to

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.600
build their entire case says he won't help
revive it in the future.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.149
They're talking, of course, about Michael
Cohen, the New York lawyer Trump used for

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:50.309
years as his family's as his family company's
trusted consiglieri, told The Daily Beast

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:55.260
he's already wasted too much of his time on
a case that slowly and then suddenly doesn't

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.540
seem to be going anywhere.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:01.930
Prosecutors only have until the current grand
jury's term expires on April 30 to issue charges,

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:06.590
at which point they must ask jurors who have
already done this for six months to continue

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:12.249
hearing evidence or call the whole thing off
and awkwardly, make the entire presentation

00:01:12.249 --> 00:01:15.920
all over again for another 23 jurors.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:19.009
If this grand jury is let go, Cohen won't
play ball.

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:23.289
Asked if he'd be willing to sit down again
with investigators or testify at a future

00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:26.920
trial against Trump, Cohen responded with
utter exasperation.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.599
Now, I've spent countless hours, 15 sessions,
including three while incarcerated.

00:01:31.599 --> 00:01:36.249
I provided thousands of documents which, coupled
with my testimony, would have been a valid

00:01:36.249 --> 00:01:39.859
basis for an indictment and charge the fact
that they have not done so.

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:45.140
Despite all of this, I'm not interested in
any further investment of my time.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.969
I have to tell you, this makes perfect, perfect
sense.

00:01:46.969 --> 00:01:51.959
Now, some people are mad at Michael Cohen
saying, wait a second, you have the knowledge,

00:01:51.959 --> 00:01:53.409
you have the information.

00:01:53.409 --> 00:01:59.840
Hell, you're the one who actually was found
guilty of crimes related to doing Trump's

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.619
bidding and now you're going to bail.

00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:06.200
But this makes 100% sense to me.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:12.400
Remember, we have now learned about the resignation
of investigators in an investigation into

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.620
Donald Trump.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.439
Why did the investigators resign?

00:02:15.439 --> 00:02:22.250
They resigned because they saw that there
was enough evidence not only to charge Trump,

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:25.700
but they felt to clearly get convictions.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.840
And yet it didn't seem to them like there
was actually any political interest in bringing

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.140
forth charges against Donald Trump.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:39.579
Why are you sitting around doing this type
of work if it's not going to go anywhere?

00:02:39.579 --> 00:02:45.489
There is a torture technique and or it's just
a way to kind of make people exasperated.

00:02:45.489 --> 00:02:46.489
Right.

00:02:46.489 --> 00:02:47.739
And we've heard about this a lot.

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:53.500
When we talk about hard labor in prison over
time in history, sometimes one thing that

00:02:53.500 --> 00:03:00.790
was done is you just have people break rocks
and then move them and then move them back.

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:06.969
And knowing that what you're doing is going
to go absolutely nowhere is absolutely demoralizing.

00:03:06.969 --> 00:03:11.900
And so I understand the investigators saying,
what are we just doing this for fun?

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.090
Is this just an academic exercise?

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:17.379
Because there seems to be no willingness to
actually charge Donald Trump.

00:03:17.379 --> 00:03:21.080
They resigned and Michael Cohen seems to be
feeling something pretty similar.

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.659
I've given you everything.

00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:24.409
I testified while incarcerated.

00:03:24.409 --> 00:03:25.489
I've provided documents.

00:03:25.489 --> 00:03:26.870
I'm give you hell.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.069
I got in trouble for the stuff that Trump
directed me to do, which was against the law.

00:03:31.069 --> 00:03:32.800
And it's going nowhere.

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.280
And the grand jury is set to end on April
30th.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:42.329
So this is very clearly one of the most blatant
political non prosecutions that I've seen

00:03:42.329 --> 00:03:46.010
in the world of national American politics.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:49.859
Cohen is at this point understandably exasperated.

00:03:49.859 --> 00:03:54.359
Multiple people around Trump have gone to
prison for crimes they did either for or in

00:03:54.359 --> 00:03:55.829
coordination with Trump.

00:03:55.829 --> 00:03:58.420
We've had multiple investigations.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.790
What what are we doing?

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.010
We've seen campaign finance violations.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:03.400
We've seen obstruction.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.120
We've seen the removal and mishandling of
classified documents.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.609
We arguably have seen election fraud, conspiracy
in.

00:04:11.609 --> 00:04:13.099
Minimum in the state of Georgia.

00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:14.860
And these are just the obvious ones.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:18.000
Let's not even talk about the multiple conspiracies
elsewhere.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:24.650
The rest of America, I think, is now seeing
the disenfranchisement that so many groups

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:25.990
have felt for a long time.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:26.990
Right.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.960
I mean, the non-rich know about the two justice
systems.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.940
Minorities know about being treated in a particular
way by police.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.840
Jews and Muslims know about religious discrimination.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.720
Remember, in the United States, when we look
at religious hate crimes, it's Jews and Muslims

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:43.860
that are primarily targeted.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:48.100
We now are all seeing exactly how this plays
out.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:52.210
So he gets treated one way and everybody else
gets treated a different way.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.639
Yep, that's exactly what's going on.

00:04:54.639 --> 00:04:58.450
So I as much as the next guy would want to
see charges brought.

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:02.569
But I understand why Michael Cohen is putting
his foot down, how much more of his life has

00:05:02.569 --> 00:05:08.449
to be devoted to testifying and giving evidence
and having lawyers himself.

00:05:08.449 --> 00:05:13.229
Remember when it's not even clear that there's
really a willingness to bring charges.

00:05:13.229 --> 00:05:14.460
So we'll see what happens.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:19.060
There's three more days until this grand jury
is done and then we'll see what happens after

00:05:19.060 --> 00:06:34.060
that.

